\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {28}{\ignorespaces GPS estimation with and without attitude compensation at $10^{\circ }$ pitch and \SI {35}{\metre } altitude. \textbf  {Left:} the naive nadir assumption projects the detection straight below the drone, producing a \SI {6.2}{\metre } systematic error equal to $h\tan \theta $. \textbf  {Right:} the attitude-compensated estimator ray-traces the detection pixel through the full rotation matrix $\mathbf  {R}$ constructed from real-time telemetry, recovering the true ground position; the residual $\sim $\SI {0.3}{\metre } error is due to IMU angular noise only ($\pm 0.5^{\circ }$).}}{75}{figure.caption.141}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:tilt-before-after}{{28}{75}{GPS estimation with and without attitude compensation at $10^{\circ }$ pitch and \SI {35}{\metre } altitude. \textbf {Left:} the naive nadir assumption projects the detection straight below the drone, producing a \SI {6.2}{\metre } systematic error equal to $h\tan \theta $. \textbf {Right:} the attitude-compensated estimator ray-traces the detection pixel through the full rotation matrix $\mathbf {R}$ constructed from real-time telemetry, recovering the true ground position; the residual $\sim $\SI {0.3}{\metre } error is due to IMU angular noise only ($\pm 0.5^{\circ }$)}{figure.caption.141}{}}
